      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T12:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So since you these referencing GPIOs directly, you should be able to use\nGPIO_DT_SPEC_GET directly without having to redefine the macro, unless you\nare expecting the GPIO flags to also include flags past the \u0027usual\u0027 Zephyr GPIO flags (like including GPIO_INPUT etc.).\nHowever I see where you are configuring the pins, you are including the\nINPUT/OUTPUT flags, so as far as I can see, it is quite OK to use the standard macro (if you were using a reference to an EC \u0027named-gpio\u0027, this wouldn\u0027t be the case, since that holds a 32 bit value for the flags).",
      "revId": "729e4e46e41a1b1bcbb2af5b40d4678101a6f7cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc987341_52f63fc0",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/include/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T22:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So there is an issue using it directly thereby this macro.\nComplains the dt_flags size\n\u003e\u003e unsigned conversion from \u0027int\u0027 to \u0027unsigned char\u0027 changes value from \u0027256\u0027 to \u00270\u0027\n\nSo I need to type cast it to get around this.",
      "parentUuid": "abea39f6_ddc94377",
      "revId": "729e4e46e41a1b1bcbb2af5b40d4678101a6f7cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0f5548b_8285ed98",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/include/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T22:43:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue here is the Brya DTS you are using for this input has flags that are larger than the 8 bits, likely GPIO_INPUT and GPIO_OUTPUT. These flags do not need to be set in that DTS declaration, but instead are set when you configure the pin.\nThe Zephyr model by convention limits the DTS GPIO flags to only the flags describing the physical properties of the pin, and in DTS there is no way of declaring an integer as a uint8, so DTS will allow flags that are \u003e 8 bits, so you will get a compilation error if the flags used can\u0027t fit in 8 bits.",
      "parentUuid": "fc987341_52f63fc0",
      "revId": "729e4e46e41a1b1bcbb2af5b40d4678101a6f7cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba6159e6_e291cf34",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/include/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T01:08:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, C code configure takes in the appropriate argument needed. But in .dts is there a way to omit out the flags, since its not being used?",
      "parentUuid": "a0f5548b_8285ed98",
      "revId": "729e4e46e41a1b1bcbb2af5b40d4678101a6f7cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d88a1b8_368d9cfa",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/include/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
